Fixes F835. At a27f8a56: _locks.py:201-222 _is_zombie returns False on OSError and ignores ps's exit code; pid_alive 166-198 returns `pid == os.getpid() or not _is_zombie(pid)`; _parent_of 264-290 also asks ps (caller _ancestry 339-355). Any macOS Seatbelt sandbox refuses /bin/ps (execvp EPERM, exit 71), so a zombie reads alive. Reproduced 2026-11-05: test__locks 138/138 plain, 136/138 under `(version 1)(allow default)`. Do NOT map "present, zombie state unreadable" to None for judge() (501-526): None falls back to age and would let a live holder older than STALE_MINUTES be taken - add a liveness answer with a basis (present-unverified counts as live). Callers to keep correct: holder_gone 498, judge 519, panel-server._pid_alive 860-863, _proc_group._gone 148-152, stamp-verification.py:3230, audit-lock.py:146, tools/_suite.py:122-129, tools/prove-gates.py:3179-3183, tests/_harness._pid_present 1655-1657 and _group_present 1660-1680 (True on OSError). Unguarded ps in tests/test__affected_tests.py:783 and 875-882. Skips use _harness.skip with the specific refusal as evidence, never any exception (F832's class.
